<article class="env-lemma" id="0EW2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EW2">Lemma <span data-tag="0EW2">38.36.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf on a site $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{ph}$ as in Topologies, Definition <a href="/tag/0DBL" data-tag="0DBL">34.8.11</a>. Let $X \to X'$ be a morphism of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{ph}$ which is a thickening. Then $\mathcal{F}(X') \to \mathcal{F}(X)$ is bijective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Observe that $X \to X'$ is a proper surjective morphism of and $X \times _{X'} X = X$. By the sheaf property for the ph covering $\{ X \to X'\} $ (Topologies, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DES" data-tag="0DES">34.8.6</a>) we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>